# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in your own values.
# .env.local is gitignored — never commit real credentials.

# --- OneMap (https://www.onemap.gov.sg) ---
# RECOMMENDED: store your account credentials and let the server mint and
# refresh access tokens automatically. Tokens expire after ~3 days, so this
# is the only setup that survives unattended on a VPS.
ONEMAP_EMAIL=
ONEMAP_PASSWORD=

# ALTERNATIVE: paste a token yourself. Simpler, but it expires in ~3 days and
# walking distances will silently revert to straight-line when it does.
# Takes precedence over the email/password pair above if set.
# ONEMAP_TOKEN=

# --- URA Data Service (optional) ---
# Official API for URA car park details WITH structured rates and coordinates.
# Free AccessKey, no card: https://eservice.ura.gov.sg/maps/api/reg.html
# Then: npm run import-ura -- --dry
URA_ACCESS_KEY=

# --- LTA DataMall (optional) ---
# Live carpark availability for COMMERCIAL and URA car parks. The data.gov.sg
# feed this app already uses covers HDB only, so without this every commercial
# card reads "No live lot data". DataMall gives free lots but not capacity, so
# those cards show "42 lots free" rather than "42 of 100".
# Free AccountKey (registration required):
# https://datamall.lta.gov.sg/content/datamall/en/request-for-api.html
LTA_DATAMALL_KEY=

# --- Web lookup (optional) ---
# When a destination has no rate and no nearby HDB carpark, the app searches the
# web for the carpark's official rates and saves them (labelled AI-retrieved).
# Two free, no-card services, kept separate so each is swappable:
#
# BOTH have fallback chains, and both should CROSS VENDORS. On 2026-08-17 the
# app went dark for the afternoon because Tavily's quota and Google's free tier
# ran out on the same day. A chain of same-vendor entries shares one quota and
# rescues nothing when that quota is the thing that failed.
#
#  1) SEARCH — Tavily does the web search (Gemini's own grounding needs billing).
#     Free key (no card): https://tavily.com
TAVILY_API_KEY=
#     Second vendor, so a Tavily outage is survivable. Free tier, no card:
#     https://brave.com/search/api  — note Brave returns result DESCRIPTIONS
#     rather than page text, so extraction is weaker; it is a spare wheel.
# BRAVE_API_KEY=
# SEARCH_PROVIDERS=tavily,brave
# SEARCH_PROVIDER=tavily        # single-provider form, if you prefer
#
#  2) EXTRACTION — an LLM turns the results into structured rates.
#     Free Gemini key (no card): https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# LLM_PROVIDER=google           # default for entries that don't name one
# LLM_MODEL=gemini-flash-latest
#
#     The chain. Entries may carry their own provider as "provider:model", and
#     for resilience they should — that is the whole point. Order best-first.
#     Overrides LLM_MODEL when set.
#
#     Cheap-first works well here because lookupCarparkRate refuses anything
#     below full confidence, so a weak answer is declined rather than stored:
# LLM_MODELS=google:gemini-flash-latest,anthropic:claude-haiku-4-5,openai:gpt-5-mini
